'' A STRUCTOR BELONGS TO THE TYPE, not to a const view of it. Mangling a 'const T'
'' produced '_ZNK2T1C1Ev' -- the CONST-METHOD spelling -- and a constructor is never
'' const, so 'dim as const T c = T( )' called a name nothing defines while the real
'' '_ZN2T1C1Ev' sat beside it. Measured: fbc emits '_ZN2T1C1Ev( &C1$0 )'.
''
'' AND AN EMPTY 'T( )' IS FINISHED once the synthesised constructor has run: it has no
'' value of its own, so the initialiser store asked it for one, got nothing, and
'' declined with the object already built. 'type<P>( 5, 6 )' is a FIELD LIST and the
'' store is what writes it -- which is why the count of what was written decides.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/const-object-init.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: _ZN2T1C1Ev
'' GOLDEN: expected/const-object-init.out
